/*
  HealthRow.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0197 · HealthRow (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source
  (components/status/HealthRow.tsx) carries almost no fixed copy: the `label` and `summary` are
  caller-supplied (already-localized) string props, and the dot + chevron are decorative. The one fixed
  string the web composes is the link `aria-label` = "{label} — {summary}".

  This surface mirrors that as a localizable FORMAT (so the separator + word order translate) and adds
  the Apple-HIG VoiceOver hints for the navigable variants — affordances the web omits but VoiceOver
  users expect on an actionable row. All keys live in the per-surface "HealthRow" table and resolve
  through the P1/S10 facade (HealthRowStrings) so the Swift sources hold no hardcoded prose; they fold
  into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time.
*/

/* --- Combined VoiceOver label (native peer of the web link aria-label) --- */
/* %1$@ = label, %2$@ = summary, e.g. "Vehicles — 12 / 12 healthy" */
"healthRow.accessibility.label" = "%1$@ — %2$@";

/* --- VoiceOver hints (shipped) --- */
"healthRow.activate.hint" = "Opens details";
"healthRow.external.hint" = "Opens in your browser";
